Safe Moza HID probe and capture commands

Tooling for the receipt-gated Moza validation lane. See docs/hardware/moza-r5-validation.md.

Usage: wheelctl moza [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init-lane
          Create a Moza R5 validation lane manifest and capture directory
  probe
          Probe connected Moza HID devices without sending FFB writes
  status
          Summarize Moza device and lane readiness without opening HID devices
  artifact-index
          Render a no-output Markdown/JSON index of Moza lane artifacts
  bench-wizard
          Render a no-output Moza bench frontier plan
  descriptor
          Capture descriptor metadata for connected Moza HID devices
  capture-input
          Capture input reports from one Moza HID device without FFB writes
  steering-stream-proof
          Record native steering angle samples from the lane R5 endpoint without output writes
  validate-capture
          Validate captured Moza input JSONL through the parser without hardware writes
  analyze-capture
          Analyze raw byte/word movement in a captured Moza input JSONL without hardware writes
  analyze-lane
          Compare required passive lane captures against idle without hardware writes
  sync-role-status
          Sync manifest logical-control semantic_status fields from stored captures
  validate-captures
          Validate every required Moza lane capture through the parser without hardware writes
  pre-output-readiness
          Summarize whether a Moza lane is ready for zero-torque or FFB output
  vendor-fake-transport
          Replay checked-in Moza vendor serial fixtures through the fake transport
  vendor-status-probe
          Send read-only Moza vendor status queries over the R5 serial interface
  vendor-status-framing-diagnosis
          Diagnose a stored Moza read-only status probe receipt without sending traffic
  vendor-status-endpoint-candidates
          Derive non-sendable authority-status endpoint correction candidates from stored evidence
  vendor-status-authority-source-gap
          Classify whether stored evidence contains a reviewed authority-state status source
  vendor-status-response-source-correlation
          Correlate stored device-to-host response samples without sending traffic
  vendor-status-response-semantic-fixtures
          Review correlated passive response fixtures without sending traffic
  vendor-status-payload-source-candidates
          Classify payload-bearing device-to-host status-source candidates without sending traffic
  vendor-status-payload-source-semantic-review
          Review payload-bearing status-source candidate fixtures without sending traffic
  vendor-status-timing-correlation-plan
          Plan the no-output timing-correlated 0x8E status-source capture
  vendor-status-timing-correlation-review
          Review passive 0x8E timing-correlation evidence without sending traffic
  vendor-status-movement-blocker-audit
          Audit the current vendor-status blocker chain without sending traffic
  authorize-vendor-authority
          Create a single-use exact Moza vendor-authority authorization receipt without sending traffic
  vendor-authority-smoke-dry-run
          Validate an exact Moza vendor-authority authorization without sending traffic
  vendor-authority-attempt
          Send one exact authorized Moza vendor-authority frame over the R5 serial interface
  vendor-post-authority-pidff-response
          Compare baseline and post-authority PIDFF response receipts without sending traffic
  vendor-protocol-evidence-review
          Review checked-in Moza vendor protocol evidence without sending traffic
  promote-fixture
          Promote a validated Moza capture JSONL into a parser fixture file
  promote-fixtures
          Promote every required Moza lane capture into parser fixture files
  zero
          Send bounded zero-torque output reports to a Moza wheelbase
  watchdog-proof
          Inject a watchdog timeout and prove the response is final zero
  disconnect-proof
          Write zero torque until a disconnect is observed, then attempt final zero
  init
          Run the staged Moza wheelbase handshake in off or standard mode
  torque-test
          Send a gated low-torque ladder after a passing real zero-torque proof
  actuator-profile-smoke
          Run a native bounded PIDFF actuator profile after steering feedback is proven
  actuator-visible-smoke
          Run a bounded native actuator smoke that must prove visible steering motion
  controlled-angle-smoke
          Preflight or run one authorized feedback-bounded native controlled-angle attempt
  pidff-lifecycle-trace
          Decode the PIDFF lifecycle recorded in a controlled-angle receipt without hardware output
  authorize-visible-output
          Authorize one exact native visible-motion retry after fresh bench-clear
  authorize-controlled-angle-output
          Authorize one exact native controlled-angle hardware attempt after fresh bench-clear
  receipt-template
          Write a non-claiming starter receipt for manual Pit House or simulator evidence
  pit-house-observation
          Write an observed Pit House UI/process state receipt
  pit-house-evidence
          Capture a no-output Pit House process/window snapshot evidence artifact
  pit-house-availability
          Capture a non-claiming Pit House install/process availability receipt
  pit-house-case
          Build one Pit House coexistence case artifact from source receipts
  pit-house-proof
          Build a Pit House coexistence receipt from observed case artifact files
  simulator-telemetry-proof
          Build a telemetry-only simulator proof receipt from normalized snapshots
  simulator-ffb-smoke
          Build a bounded simulator-to-Moza FFB smoke proof from output logs
  promote-manifest
          Promote manifest completion state only after a live bundle verification passes
  verify-bundle
          Verify a Moza hardware lane receipt bundle before claiming readiness
  audit-lane
          Audit stored verification and manifest-promotion receipts after promotion
  help
          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Output in JSON format for machine parsing

  -v, --verbose...
          Verbose logging

      --no-mock
          Fail if wheeld is unreachable instead of showing simulated data [env: WHEELCTL_NO_MOCK=1]

      --endpoint <ENDPOINT>
          Service endpoint (for testing)

          [env: WHEELCTL_ENDPOINT=]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
